## 🔒 3. Local Git Hooks & Protection
To preserve architecture integrity, client hooks prevent user error before data ever hits your upstream host repository.
## pre-push Hook
Installed during bootstrapping to .git/hooks/pre-push, this stops accidental direct commits or force-pushes targeting your protected main channel:

#!/usr/bin/env bash# .git/hooks/pre-push
while read local_ref local_sha remote_ref remote_shado
    if [[ "$remote_ref" == "refs/heads/main" ]]; then
        echo "❌ [GitOps Error]: Direct pushes to 'main' are completely protected!"
        echo "Please push to your specific host branch and submit a PR."
        exit 1
    fidone

