## 🔋 4. Event-Driven Continuous Synchronization
Instead of running battery-draining continuous background scripts, synchronization logic leverages native hardware hooks.
## Linux Engine: udev + systemd Interception
Hardware status fluctuations broadcast system interrupts. We grab those events to fire off our custom Git-sync agent without consuming idling CPU cycles.
## 1. The Kernel Triggers (/etc/udev/rules.d/99-battery-gitops.rules)

# Sync on Charger Connection Alterations (Plugged/Unplugged)
SUBSYSTEM=="power_supply", ENV{POWER_SUPPLY_NAME}=="AC", ACTION=="change", RUN+="/usr/bin/systemctl --no-block --user -M YOUR_USERNAME start gitops-power-sync.service"

# Sync immediately when battery drains down or charges up to exactly 50%
SUBSYSTEM=="power_supply", ENV{POWER_SUPPLY_NAME}=="BAT0", ENV{POWER_SUPPLY_CAPACITY}=="50", ACTION=="change", RUN+="/usr/bin/systemctl --no-block --user -M YOUR_USERNAME start gitops-power-sync.service"

## 2. The Service Manifest (~/.config/systemd/user/gitops-power-sync.service)

[Unit]
Description=Trigger Dotfiles Synchronization on Environment Change
After=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/home/%u/.dotfiles/scripts/git-sync-host

[Install]
WantedBy=default.target

(Enabled via systemctl --user enable gitops-power-sync.service to naturally ensure execution at boot/login).
## Windows Engine: PowerShell + Task Scheduler
Windows nodes query power infrastructures natively by mounting into the WMI subsystem, managed using hardware metrics conditions inside the OS Task Scheduler.
## The Sync Command Script ($HOME/.dotfiles/scripts/git-sync-host.ps1)

# Stop syncing if we drop to battery power
$Battery = (Get-CimInstance -ClassName Win32_Battery).BatteryStatusif ($Battery -and $Battery -eq 1) { exit 0 }
# Ensure network visibility if (-not (Test-Connection -ComputerName 8.8.8.8 -Count 1 -Quiet)) { exit 0 }

$CurrentBranch = (git symbolic-ref --short HEAD)
git fetch origin
git pull --rebase origin main
if (git status --porcelain) {
    git add .
    git commit -m "Automated state checkpoint: $(Get-Date)"
    git push origin "$CurrentBranch"
}


* Trigger Mechanics: Routed inside Windows Task Scheduler configured to execute At Logon and Every 1 Hour, utilizing the Task Condition: "Start the task only if the computer is on AC power".

