## 🧪 5. CI/CD Validation Pipeline
Every Pull Request moving from a personal host-* sandbox branch toward the protected main branch undergoes automated validation inside GitHub Actions before integration.
## CI Goals

* Shell Verification: Linting bash configurations and orchestration files via ShellCheck.
* Dry-Run Deployments: Firing up clean virtual runtimes to check that the installation script functions flawlessly on a pristine host.

# .github/workflows/dotfiles-validation.ymlname: Dotfiles GitOps CI
on:
  pull_request:
    branches: [ main ]
jobs:
  lint:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: ShellCheck Linting
        uses: ludeeus/action-shellcheck@master
        with:
          scandir: './scripts'

  test-bootstrap-linux:
    needs: lint
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: Verify Installer Run
        run: |
          chmod +x ./scripts/bootstrap.sh
          # Mock inputs for non-interactive CI execution
          echo "ci-test-runner" | ./scripts/bootstrap.sh

