## 🏁 How to Use This Repository## Setting up a new machine
Simply clone down your base configuration environment repository and spin up the internal installation orchestrator:

git clone https://github.com ~/.dotfiles
cd ~/.dotfiles
chmod +x scripts/bootstrap.sh
./scripts/bootstrap.sh

## Propagating a global configuration change

   1. Navigate to your local machine repository.
   2. Make your edits to the specific configurations (e.g., adding an alias inside zsh/.zshrc).
   3. Commit the change locally to your safe host sandbox environment.
   4. Push your changes and open a clean Pull Request to main on GitHub.
   5. Once your CI checks pass and you merge the PR, all other online systems will pull down the fresh global change automatically on their next hardware event trigger!

